  "doc.title": "How a CPU's Three Levels of Cache Work · a long essay you can play with",
  "doc.desc": "Memory takes tens of nanoseconds and a CPU does several things every nanosecond. How do caches of tens of kilobytes to tens of megabytes keep it from waiting most of the time? Why three levels, and why is each the size it is? Ten cache models run on real address traces: splitting an address, associativity and the three kinds of miss, LRU and RRIP, write-back and write buffers, inclusive and exclusive levels, the limit on L1 size, prefetching, MESI and false sharing, and the latency staircase of a pointer chase.",
  "nav.back": "← Knowledge index",
